From: Julian Andres Klode <julian.klode@canonical.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:34:52 +0200
Subject: upki fetch: Refuse to run as root

Fetching as root would leave root-owned files in the revocation cache that the unprivileged fetch service can then no longer update.  Tell the user to start upki-fetch.service instead.  The check uses libc::geteuid() on unix and is a no-op elsewhere.
